the iconography as part of a wider repertoire shared with other Minoan signet 
rings and glyptic objects. [5][9]\n\nSome methodological analyses classify the 
Ring of Nestor among \"gemmae dubitandae\", or doubtful engraved gems, 
emphasizing that its archaeological context is not securely documented and that 
